 Looking at your `inference.module.js` code, I can see the issue:

In `updateForm()`:
```javascript
export const updateForm = async (eventData) => {
  const selectedProviderName = eventData.target.value;
  const updatedTree = buildFormTree(selectedProviderName);
  await runtime.call('ui.showModal', { tree: updatedTree });
  runtime.log(`[Inference] Form updated for provider: ${selectedProviderName}`);
};
```

And in `buildFormTree()`:
```javascript
const buildFormTree = (selectedProviderName = '') => {
  // ...
  "provider-select": { 
    // ...
    value: selectedProviderName, 
    // ...
  },
```

The logic looks correct - `selectedProviderName` should be getting the new value from `eventData.target.value` and passing it to set the select's value.

**But there's an issue with the showModal call:** You're only passing `tree`, but `showModal` expects a full object with title, content, etc.

It should be:
```javascript
await runtime.call('ui.showModal', { 
  title: "Configure AI Provider & Model", 
  tree: updatedTree 
});
```

Without the title, the modal structure might not be rebuilding correctly, causing the form to reset instead of preserving the selected value.

