The problem is in `setOtherProps`. The `disabled` property isn't in `specialProps`, so it's getting set as an HTML attribute instead of a DOM property:

```javascript
el.setAttribute('disabled', false) // This still disables the element!
```

In HTML, any `disabled` attribute disables the element regardless of its value. You need to set the DOM property instead.

**Fix:** Add `disabled` to `specialProps` and handle it properly in `setFormProps`:

```javascript
const specialProps = new Set(['tag', 'text', 'class', 'id', 'events', 'data', 'name', 'type', 'value', 'placeholder', 'required', 'options', 'focus', 'disabled']);

const setFormProps = (el, node) => {
    ['name', 'type', 'value', 'placeholder', 'required'].forEach(prop => node[prop] && (el[prop] = node[prop]));
    if ('disabled' in node) el.disabled = node.disabled;
};
```

